    "chunk_text": "proceeds of committing theft. Notwithstanding anything to the\n\ncontrary in this Act, he shall be entitled to take action in terms of\n\nCode of Criminal Procedure Act to take such property into his\n\npossession and take further action in terms of the law.\n\n5\n\n10\n\n15\n\n20\n\n25\n\n30\n\n80Proceeds of Crime\n\n(9) Subject to necessary authorization that may have to be obtained from the competent authorities of a foreign country and subject to administrative approval, an Investigation O\ufb03 cer shall be entitled to carry out the entire or part of an investigation under this Act in a foreign country. For such purpose, an Investigation O\ufb03 cer may obtain the assistance of a law enforcement o\ufb03 cer of such foreign country.\n\n(10) Where a law enforcement o\ufb03 cer of a foreign country provides assistance to an Investigation O\ufb03 cer and therefor conducts any investigation pertaining to suspected proceeds of crime, it shall be deemed that such investigation or part thereof was conducted by an Investigation O\ufb03 cer, and evidence may be presented in judicial proceedings founded upon material collected by such foreign law enforcement o\ufb03 cer.\n\nClari\ufb01 cation:\n\nFor the purpose of obtaining the assistance of a foreign law\n\nenforcement o\ufb03 cer in the conduct of an investigation in a\n\nforeign country, an Investigation O\ufb03 cer need not have been\n\npresent in such foreign country when the relevant part of the\n\ninvestigation was being conducted.\n\n(11) The Designated O\ufb03 cers and Investigation O\ufb03 cers of Sri Lanka Police and the Commission to Investigate Allegations of Bribery or Corruption shall take appropriate measures for the protection and preservation of information and other material received by such o\ufb03 cers under this Act and gathered in course of an investigation. Such information and material shall be used only under the provisions of this Act for the purposes set out in the Act.\n\n5\n\n10\n\n15\n\n20\n\n25\n\n81Proceeds of Crime"
